# Real findings that are not secrets, and why.
#
# Every one has been read. None of them opens anything that exists.
#
# This project connects to a mailbox, so the word the gate looks for is bound
# to appear: in a field of a type, in a read of an environment variable, and in
# an invented value inside a check. None of the three is a credential. The
# mailbox it actually connects to here is an invented IMAP server that accepts
# anybody and listens only on 127.0.0.1.
#
# The read from the environment is the opposite of a secret in the code:
# IMAP_PASSWORD takes precedence over whatever is in the address, because a
# password inside a URL ends up in the shell history and in the process list.
#
# This never covers company names or real keys: those block from any file.
#
# A note for whoever writes here next: a reason must not reproduce the code it
# excuses. This file is reviewed like every other one.

packages/server/src/imap/client.ts    # the field of the type, and the read from the environment that takes precedence over the address
packages/server/test/imap.test.ts     # an invented value, to prove the environment really wins
